&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diagnostics &amp;amp; Repair:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct hardware and network diagnostics on live and offline systems. Troubleshoot issues reported through tickets, replace components, and perform physical repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equipment Deployment:&lt;/strong&gt; Support equipment installations, device provisioning, and operating system installations, taking on more complex troubleshooting and deployment work as your experience grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Cabling &amp;amp; Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain high standards of cable management and structured cabling, and follow physical and cybersecurity protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain accurate inventory records and ticket updates. Contribute to standard operating procedures (SOPs), technical documentation, and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Knowledge Sharing:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with local and cross-functional teams to support operational readiness. Share knowledge and contribute to team training and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call &amp;amp; Response:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in a rotating on-call schedule and be available to arrive on-site within 60 minutes when an incident requires hands-on support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Foundation:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience or coursework in computer hardware assembly, installation, and physical and logical troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating Systems &amp;amp; Networking:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with Linux operating systems and fundamental networking concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving &amp;amp; Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to follow established procedures, prioritize tasks, troubleshoot technical issues, and recognize when to ask for guidance or escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Teamwork:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong organizational and communication skills, a collaborative and curious mindset, and a commitment to high reliability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Willingness to build technical skills, learn new systems, and take on responsibilities that match your experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to perform the following essential duties, with or without reasonable accommodation:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move and position equipment weighing up to 50 lbs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain in a stationary position for extended periods while performing diagnostics and repairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access equipment in confined spaces, under-floor areas, and on ladders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle small hardware components, connectors, and cabling with precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in data center environments with hot/cold aisle temperatures ranging from 60°F to 90°F.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
