&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant project or program management experience in data center, mission-critical, or large-scale capital development, preferably on the owner’s side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of significant pre-construction workstreams, including integrated schedule management and budget tracking for land acquisition, site development, or construction readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of entitlement and permitting processes, including AHJ submittals and approval sequencing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating due diligence workstreams—including title, survey, geotechnical, and environmental reviews—and tracking closing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive follow-through on agreed deliverables across internal teams and external parties without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with project controls and reporting tools such as Smartsheet, Microsoft Project, Primavera P6, or equivalent, and the ability to turn project information into clear executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating consultant agreements, statements of work, purchase orders, and invoice validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment in identifying risks, managing dependencies, and escalating decisions to project leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, construction management, real estate, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to project sites as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
