&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) licensure, or certifications such as LEED, Uptime Institute, or similar industry qualifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify, evaluate, and implement emerging data center technologies, particularly for high-density compute, advanced cooling, liquid cooling, power distribution, controls, modular infrastructure, and energy efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to keep a portfolio-level perspective while engaging directly in the details needed to resolve critical project issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bring structure to ambiguity and translate technical and business requirements into actionable project plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify developing risks early, set practical mitigation strategies, and communicate recommendations confidently to senior and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building productive relationships among internal teams, data center providers, A/E firms, contractors, consultants, and equipment suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
