&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a team that is scaling as fast as the business it accounts for. We solve problems quickly, learn and improve as we go, and operate with positive intent, flexibility, and patience. This is a hands-on team that runs a monthly close and builds the process at the same time — teamwork and clear communication matter as much as execution. We win together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manager, DC Construction - Project Accounting owns the accounting for capital costs from the point a project is set up through the point completed assets are placed in service. You will own the construction in progress (CIP) ledger for your projects — how cost is captured, how it accumulates against each element of the build, and how it clears into the fixed asset register when an asset is ready for its intended use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, execution-oriented role at the center of our self-build and fit-out programs. You will set up the project structure that cost flows through, run the monthly accrual and cost-to-complete process, determine when assets are ready for their intended use, and trigger their capitalization on a timely basis. You will partner closely with teams across accounting, finance, construction and operations, and maintain the documentation and controls that support internal and external audit. This role reports to the Senior Manager, Construction Accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Setup &amp;amp; Cost Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the setup of the project structure and hierarchy through which capital cost is captured, so that cost lands against the correct project, phase, building and data hall&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain the mapping that lets construction cost be analyzed by element of the build (e.g., shell versus data hall) and built up into assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the systems and transformation teams on project costing configuration in NetSuite and the interface to SiteTracker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Construction in Progress &amp;amp; Cost Accumulation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the CIP ledger for your projects — the capture and accumulation of materials, contractor, service and other capital cost as it is incurred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply capitalization policy to determine which costs are eligible by project phase, and document the basis for cost classification decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the monthly CIP rollforward and supporting tie-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open-PO Accruals &amp;amp; Cost-to-Complete&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly open purchase order and construction accrual process, including the reversal and re-establishment of accruals carried from prior periods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the cost-to-complete view for each project and reconcile committed and incurred cost against budget and forecast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve reconciling and outstanding items on a timely basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Servicing &amp;amp; Capitalization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine when assets are ready for their intended use and ensure they are placed in service on a timely basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the capitalization of completed assets out of CIP and into the fixed asset register, including the unitization of cost into asset records and the assignment of asset class and initial useful life at capitalization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the completeness and accuracy of asset records created in the period and the tie-out of in-service activity, in partnership with the property accounting team who maintain the standing register&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the accounting interface to the construction, operations, leasing, corporate accounting and financial planning teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with construction and operations to validate asset readiness and support the accuracy of in-service dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide the project-level cost information required by downstream reporting, systems and audit stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls, Audit &amp;amp; Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain process documentation and controls to meet Sarbanes-Oxley 404 requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate internal and external audits and respond to information requests on a timely basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead process improvements, including automation opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation and testing of new and enhanced financial systems, including project costing and asset management tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of accounting experience, with a strong background in capital, construction or fixed asset accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning a month-end close process end to end, delivered to deadline every cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the accounting for capital projects — CIP, cost capitalization, accruals, and the transfer of completed assets into service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of US GAAP and SOX compliance, with proven experience owning control documentation and supporting external audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work cross-functionally with non-accounting teams, including construction and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP systems experience required; experience with NetSuite, project costing modules, and close and controls management software is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain momentum in high-growth environments, including the capacity to act effectively when faced with ambiguity or incomplete data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational, time and self-management skills, and the ability to prioritize and work well under pressure to meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applicants must have work authorization that does not require sponsorship from the company now or in the future&lt;/li&gt;
