&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;The Hardware Quality &amp;amp; Operations organization at CoreWeave is responsible for delivering reliable, high-performance hardware infrastructure at scale. The team partners across engineering, product lifecycle management, supply chain, manufacturing, and quality to ensure new products and sustaining production lines are ready to build, test, and operate successfully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is seeking an experienced Staff Manufacturing Operations Program Manager to join the Hardware Quality &amp;amp; Operations organization. This role will focus on manufacturing execution and transformation across new product introduction (NPI) and sustaining operations. You will lead cross-organizational build and test readiness alignment across NPI phases, drive sustaining program management, identify and mitigate risk, facilitate quality excursion oversight, and serve as a central point of alignment across engineering, PLM, supply chain, manufacturing, and quality stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;This is a highly cross-functional, execution-focused role for someone who is comfortable bringing structure to ambiguity, translating technical risk into business impact, and holding technical teams accountable to program milestones across new product ramps and mature production lines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Manufacturing Program Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Define and own the NPI manufacturing program plan across EVT, DVT, PVT, and MP phases, including schedule, build and test readiness, exit criteria, and go/no-go gate reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Own the transition from NPI to sustaining, ensuring process documentation, quality plans, spares strategy, and open action items are handed off cleanly to steady-state production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Stand up and maintain risk registers covering technical, supply chain, quality, and schedule risks across contract manufacturers, suppliers, and data centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Own readiness reviews for changes introduced into active production lines, ensuring changes are validated and risk-assessed before rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Supply Chain Strategy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Manage manufacturing strategies encompassing contract manufacturer expansion, data enablement, and cross-contract-manufacturer standardization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Lead the evolution of the Hardware Quality metrics framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Communication and Alignment&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;wnfdntf&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Act as a primary point of alignment across engineering, manufacturing, supply chain, quality, and program and product management for assigned NPI and sustaining programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Prepare and deliver executive-level program updates, including status, risks, and decisions needed, to leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdnte _1ibi0s33w&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Build consensus across teams with competing priorities and drive decisions to closure when programs are at risk, whether during a new product ramp or a live production issue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience in program management, NPI, operations, or quality within hardware manufacturing environments, spanning both new product launches and sustaining or steady-state production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ownership of NPI programs through EVT, DVT, PVT, and MP build phases, with direct experience driving build and test readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Experience managing sustaining engineering programs, including ECOs, running changes, second-source qualification, or end-of-life and product transition planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;A track record of facilitating cross-functional resolution of quality issues under time pressure, both during fast-moving NPI ramps and in live production environments, without formal authority over the teams involved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Excellent structured communication skills, with the ability to present program status and risk to senior leadership and drive alignment across technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Strong program and project management fundamentals, including schedule management, risk tracking, milestone and gate reviews, and action item management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Experience working with supply chain, contract manufacturers, or ODM/OEM partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Engineering, Operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Preferred&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;12+ years of direct experience in program management, NPI, operations, or quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Deep understanding of server architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Familiarity with PLM and ERP systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Strong working knowledge of quality tools and methodologies, including FMEA, 8D, CAPA, root cause analysis, and containment and corrective action processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;A strong history of building processes and systems that add structure across organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit?&amp;nbsp;We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match.&amp;nbsp;Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team.&amp;nbsp;If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;You’re comfortable driving execution across complex, cross-functional hardware programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;You’re curious about how manufacturing, quality, supply chain, and engineering systems work together at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;You’re an expert at translating technical risk into clear decisions and measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;wnfdnti _1ibi0s33y _1ibi0s34u&quot;&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp;We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on.&amp;nbsp;We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning.&amp;nbsp;Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;wnfdntu _1ibi0s3f5 _1ibi0s3ce _1ibi0s3ea&quot;&gt;The base salary range for this role is $207,000 to $275,000. The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range we’ve posted represents the typical compensation range for this role. To determine actual compensation, we review the market rate for each candidate which can include a variety of factors. These include qualifications, experience, interview performance, and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs. The benefits below reflect our US-based offerings for full-time employees; for roles in other locations, benefits vary and are shared during the hiring process. These include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
