&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave’s North America Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS) team is responsible for ensuring safe, compliant, and audit-ready operations across all owned, leased, colocation, and build-to-suit data center and warehouse facilities in the U.S. and Canada. The team translates CoreWeave’s Global EHS strategy into an auditable program that supports 24/7 mission-critical operations, high-growth construction and commissioning activity, and a rapidly expanding real estate footprint - partnering closely with Data Center Operations, Design &amp;amp; Construction, Critical Engineering/Facilities, Corporate Security, Sustainability, Legal, People, and Procurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own site compliance across all EHS programs, training, reporting, and recordkeeping within CoreWeave’s management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive shared ownership of EHS across North America, embedding metrics into operational dashboards to hold teams accountable to EHS performance objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure audit readiness for government agencies, ISO certifications, and customer audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chair or co-chair a regional EHS governance forum bringing together site, construction, and operations stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee regulatory interactions, recordkeeping, and reporting across all U.S. states and Canadian provinces where CoreWeave operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional incident reporting, investigation, and root-cause analysis, ensuring timely notification per company and regulatory timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and exercise site emergency response, business continuity, and crisis communication plans with Security and site leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track leading and lagging indicators and report trends, including KPI dashboards, to regional and global leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a proactive safety culture, including hazard reporting, stop-work authority, and recognition programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage regional budget and staffing plans and a network of third-party EHS service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a 24/7/365 on-call posture for mission-critical incident response and regulatory notification support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary liaison with regulatory agencies, first responders, and insurance/risk partners across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Occupational Safety, Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety, Environmental Science, Engineering, or a related field required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of progressive EHS experience, including at least 5 years in a multi-site or regional leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting data centers, mission-critical facilities, or other 24/7 high-hazard industrial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing EHS programs across multiple U.S. states, with direct experience managing regulatory engagement with federal, state, and local agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required certification: Certified Safety Professional (CSP), Certified Industrial Hygienist (CIH), Associate Safety Professional (ASP), Certified Hazardous Materials Manager (CHMM), Occupational Health and Safety Technologist (OHST), or NEBOSH qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High EHS technical proficiency, with proficiency using an enterprise EHS management information system and data-driven reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills, with experience presenting to senior leadership, and the ability to prioritize across multiple workstreams in a matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel approximately 40-60% of the time, including domestic U.S. and Canada travel, and to walk data center floors, mechanical/electrical yards, and construction sites using required personal protective equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Occupational Safety, Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety, Environmental Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing EHS programs across Canadian provinces, in addition to multiple U.S. states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain site-specific security or facility access clearances, including FedRAMP-supported government operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
