&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Business Partner for Product and Engineering, you’ll enable leaders to make data-driven people decisions that support execution and growth.&amp;nbsp;You’ll own and drive core people processes, balancing executional rigor with speed. You’ll identify patterns early, surface insights quickly, and help leaders course-correct before people challenges impact delivery.&amp;nbsp;The focus of this role is reducing friction, increasing clarity, and amplifying leadership impact as the organization scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the center of CoreWeave&#39;s Product and Engineering organization, partnering with senior leaders through a period of rapid growth and increasing complexity. This is not a role where you wait to be asked, you bring a clear point of view, operate independently across complex situations, and are embedded deeply enough in the business to anticipate what leaders need before they articulate it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You think about the upstream and downstream implications of every recommendation, build trusted relationships through coaching and knowledge sharing, and consistently deliver high-quality outcomes even in ambiguous or fast-moving environments. This person shapes initiatives, refines how people work gets done across P&amp;amp;E, and elevates the quality of decisions across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role means turning priorities into practical, scalable solutions that help Product and Engineering operate effectively—and leaving the function better than you found it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Investing in our people is one of our top priorities, and we value candidates who can bring their diversified experiences to our teams. Here are some qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. We&#39;d love to talk about whether this aligns with your experience and interests and what you’re excited to work on next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your impact will be felt across various dimensions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
