&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a Senior Security Engineer to own key technical work in CoreWeave’s Vulnerability Management program. You will build and improve triage, prioritization, and remediation-tracking systems across application, infrastructure, and hardware domains. You will deliver well-scoped projects, contribute to technical standards, and work closely with senior engineers and stakeholders to drive execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own VM technical projects end to end and contribute to architecture decisions for your areas of the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain triage automation, including integrations, decision logic, and production hardening&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement workflow components from assessment and detection to ticket routing and remediation tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and triage hardware-adjacent vulnerabilities (GPU firmware, DPU firmware/BlueField, and BMC surfaces) alongside senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support response to embargoed disclosures and zero-day events, working with owner teams that deploy fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to prioritization logic, severity models, and exception workflows through code, design reviews, and technical proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build technical metrics and risk reporting that inform program and leadership decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in root-cause analysis for vulnerability incidents and implement technical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge through code reviews and documentation, and help onboard new teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with security, engineering, and operational stakeholders to improve workflow reliability and speed up remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in vulnerability management, application security, platform security, or cloud security engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building security automation (SOAR workflows, AI/ML systems, detection pipelines) in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of vulnerability management best practices: CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV, threat intelligence integration, and risk-based prioritization frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong development background, with coding skills in Python, Go, or similar languages for building production-grade security systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with modern vulnerability management tooling (for example Wiz, Semgrep, Rapid7, Tenable, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with specialized infrastructure (GPU/DPU environments, firmware security, hardware vulnerabilities, or high-performance computing) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of collaborating across teams to deliver technical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how security decisions affect engineering velocity, customer trust, and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI/ML-powered security systems (LLM integration, automated decision-making, human-in-the-loop validation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to hardware vendor security work (embargoed disclosures and pre-release collaboration)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security automation platforms such as TINES and serverless frameworks (AWS Lambda, GCP Cloud Functions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps, DevSecOps, or SRE background with experience in AWS/GCP/Azure cloud services and Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, CloudFormation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Kubernetes security (container scanning, admission controllers, supply chain security, runtime protection)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-growing startup or cloud-native environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing vulnerabilities in a FedRAMP-certified environment or under similar regulatory frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
