&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Cloud Platform API team&lt;/strong&gt; builds the platform and infrastructure that front CoreWeave&#39;s control plane. This role sits with the group that owns the &lt;strong&gt;API Gateway&lt;/strong&gt; (the single secure front door for control-plane traffic) and the &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Gateway&lt;/strong&gt;, one secure endpoint into every CoreWeave Kubernetes Service (CKS) cluster control plane, public or private. The team runs the &lt;strong&gt;Envoy&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Gateway API&lt;/strong&gt; stack that carries every customer, CLI, console, and Terraform request. This is high-leverage infrastructure at CoreWeave: the gateway is the choke point, and its latency and availability are what customers perceive as the platform&#39;s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Engineer on the Cloud Platform API team, you&#39;ll design and operate the gateways that front the entire control plane. You&#39;ll drive large-scale networking migrations, such as moving from NGINX/HAProxy to Envoy across every zone with no customer-visible regression, and own routing, TLS/mTLS, rate limiting, and observability across the stack. You&#39;ll set technical direction for how the team runs its infrastructure, anticipate problems before they turn into incidents, and help stand up new customer-facing features for this infra. You&#39;ll also mentor other engineers, lead post-mortems, and act as a trusted advisor across teams like CKS, VPC, IAM, Cloud Console, and more. This role sits on a technical-leadership track, and we especially welcome engineers interested in eventually leading or managing a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the API and Kubernetes Gateways API stacks and their CRDs: routing, TLS/mTLS, rate limiting, and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive large-scale infrastructure migrations (for example, HAProxy → Envoy) across every zone with one audit-log shape and no customer-visible regression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage networking and traffic at scale: L4/L7 proxying, load balancing, global routing, live failover to healthy backends, encrypted transport, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction across the gateway stack and define the engineering standards the team follows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor senior and mid-level engineers, lead post-mortems, and act as a bridge across teams and to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience writing &lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with &lt;strong&gt;networking and traffic infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;: L4/L7 load balancing, reverse proxies (Envoy, HAProxy, or NGINX), or API gateways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt; experience, ideally with the Gateway API or Ingress, operators and controllers, and running multiple clusters and the applications deployed across them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong grounding in &lt;strong&gt;TLS/mTLS&lt;/strong&gt; and edge and authentication concerns, plus performance tuning of network-facing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of &lt;strong&gt;setting technical direction&lt;/strong&gt; and leading initiatives across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication about your technical contributions and cross-team collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building and operating backend systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors degree in Computer Science or equivalent professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Preferred:&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a large-scale infrastructure migration end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a high-traffic edge or gateway as a production choke point: monitoring, runbooks, and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with certificate issuance and rotation (for example, via Vault) and with multi-zone or federated control planes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in a technical-leadership or engineering-management path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience building and operating backend systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
